  "caption": "Quinn went full barefoot on hard tiles at home. A week later, the middle of the heel felt like a deep bruise, worse after a long day standing.\n\nThat pattern can point to an irritated heel fat pad, the heel's natural cushion. It's different from plantar heel pain, which tends to be worst with the first steps in the morning.\n\nWhat can help: cushion it with heel cups, gel pads or well-padded shoes, wear slippers on hard floors, swap some concrete walking or running for swimming or cycling, use mats at standing jobs, and build calf and foot strength. Recovery is often slow, around 6–12 weeks.\n\nSevere pain, pain after a fall from height, numbness, or no change with cushioning is worth getting checked.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
